From 27b9052faa100a562a1c4a0bc96b8c5756cab731 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TrinityXSX <trinityxsx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:04:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Serve a keyboard and mouse page, and pick the PC input in the
 profile

[input] remote = off | sender | browser chooses how a PC's keyboard and
mouse reach the game (off by default: no port is open). The title reads
the profile again every two seconds, so TrinityXSX's settings switch it
while it runs, and writes <data>/netinput.txt (the mode, and the page's
address and PIN) for the library to show.

browser: src/pw_webinput.c serves the capture page (src/pw_webinput_page.c,
generated from TrinityXSX's tools/netinput-sender/src/web/index.html) and
a WebSocket on TCP 8361 to private addresses only. The WebSocket wants
the PIN the in-game menu shows (fresh each start), an IPv4 Host and the
page's own Origin; wrong PINs lock it out for a while. Its text commands
(on, off, h, k, b, m, w) become input through pw_netinput_set, which
folds and diffs as the other sources do; a stop, a closed page or a
silent capturing one releases everything. native/pw_webinput_ps5.c is the
non-blocking libSceNet side, and finds the console's address with a
connected UDP socket (no libSceNetCtl).

sender: the TXIN datagrams of patch 0012, now opened and closed with the
mode (pw_netinput_ps5_close releases what was held).
